---
import OutcomeBar from './OutcomeBar.astro';
import { headline, kinds, outcomeTotal, outcomes, systemChips, trapTypes, world } from './model';
---
<section class="rule" id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
    <h2>A whole company of tools, and tasks that need several of them</h2>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="card step">
        <span class="num">01</span>
        <h3>Realistic systems, one consistent world</h3>
        <p>Harbour &amp; Vale Retail Group is a fictional UK homewares and fashion retailer. Its {world.systems} systems share master data, so a supplier's spend or a shipment's ETA agrees wherever it appears. The data is generated and reproducible: every run starts from the same state.</p>
        <div class="viz">
          <ul class="pills">
            {systemChips.map((s) => <li title={s.name}>{s.short}</li>)}
            <li class="more">{world.systems} systems in all</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card step">
        <span class="num">02</span>
        <h3>Tasks and traps from persona questions</h3>
        <p>Each task is a question a real role would ask, with follow-ups, or a lookup in one system. Traps test what a careful model should notice: data that isn't there, actions that need approval, instructions hidden in tool output.</p>
        <div class="viz">
          <p class="vlabel">One example run: {world.tasks} tasks</p>
          <div class="kbar" aria-hidden="true">{kinds.map((k) => <i class={`k k-${k.key}`} style={`flex:${k.n} 1 0`} />)}</div>
          <ul class="leg">{kinds.map((k) => <li><i class={`k k-${k.key}`} />{k.label} <b>{k.n}</b></li>)}</ul>
          <p class="vlabel">Trap types</p>
          <ul class="pills dim">{trapTypes.map((t) => <li>{t}</li>)}</ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card step">
        <span class="num">03</span>
        <h3>Graded by checks plus a judge</h3>
        <p>Code checks every fact and write against the tool calls; a judge reads the conversation. Reports lead with why tasks fail, not just how many.</p>
        <div class="viz">
          <p class="vlabel">{headline.names.a}'s {outcomeTotal} tasks by outcome</p>
          <div class="obar" aria-hidden="true"><OutcomeBar /></div>
          <ul class="olist">
            {outcomes.map((o) => (
              <li><span class="chip" style={`--c:var(--mm-o-${o.key})`}><i />{o.name}</span><span class="o-d">{o.text}</span><span class="o-n">{o.n}</span></li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
